.claude/worktrees/
logs/

# design-sync (claude.ai/design): staged converter scripts, build output,
# machine state. The durable set under .design-sync/ IS committed.
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
.design-sync/.cache/
.design-sync/learnings/
.design-sync/node_modules

# Generated by scripts/build-stimulus-plates.py. Deliberately NOT committed:
# merging to main deploys the repo root to Vercel production, so a committed
# specimen sheet would become a public page on the live site.
stimulus-plates.html
__pycache__/
figure-vocabulary.html
plot-spec-dictionary.html
renderer-eval.html
figure-directions.html
shots/
exam-composition.html
shots2/
# figure-system.html is the design system's own page — the one that shows what
# each family IS. Committed and served for the same reason pie-directions.html
# is: a page nobody can open is a page nobody checks, and that is how a specimen
# sheet drifted twenty selectors from what ships. Carries noindex.
!scripts/figure-system.html
figure-system.html
shots3/
shots4/
e2e-preview*.html
e2e-payload*.json
exam-ui-preview.html
shots5/

# Written by scripts/check-desmos-activation.cjs during a live activation run.
# Never committed: it is a screenshot of a licensed third-party calculator.
scripts/desmos-activation.png

# Rendered by scripts/check-visual-fidelity.cjs on every run, for looking at.
# The BASELINES (tests/visual-baselines/) are committed; these are the current
# renders and the diffs against them, and they are rewritten each time.
tests/visual-out/
# pie-directions.html is the exception: every other generated page here is
# ignored, and the consequence is that none of them has ever been deployable —
# they could only ever be reviewed through screenshots someone pasted. A design
# decision is taken by LOOKING at the thing on the real site, so this one is
# committed and served. It carries noindex; it is not public-site surface.
!scripts/pie-directions.html
pie-directions.html
